===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A piece of information describing, or an [[account]] of certain [[event]]s given or presented to someone, with the most common [[adposition]]s being [[by]] (referring to creator of the report) and [[on]] (referring to the subject).
#: {{ux|en|A '''report''' by the telecommunications ministry on the phone network revealed a severe capacity problem.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 16, 2011|author=Denis Campbell|title=Hospital staff 'lack skills to cope with dementia patients'| work=Guardian| url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/society/2011/dec/16/hospital-staff-dementia-patients| passage=Hospitals are failing to care properly for the growing number of people with dementia, according to an NHS-funded '''report''', which has prompted demands for big improvements to help patients.}}
# [[reputation|Reputation]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Sonnets|sonnet=36|text=I love thee in such sort / As, thou being mine, mine is thy good '''report'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1902|author=John Buchan|title=The Outgoing of the Tide
|passage=Certain it is that if he had been daft before, he now ran wild in his pranks, and an evil '''report''' of him was in every mouth.}}
# {{lb|en|firearms}} The [[sharp]], loud sound from a [[gun]] or explosion.
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|[[s:Moby-Dick/Chapter 34|chapter 34]]|text=While their masters, the mates, seemed afraid of the sound of the hinges of their own jaws, the harpooneers chewed their food with such a relish that there was a '''report''' to it.}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Treasure Island|text={{...}} a pistol-shot, flash and '''report''', came from the hedge-side.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|title=s:en:The Coup de Grâce
|year=1889
|author=w:Ambrose Bierce
|passage= He knelt upon one knee, cocked the weapon, placed the muzzle against the man's forehead, and turning away his eyes pulled the trigger. There was no '''report'''. He had used his last cartridge for the horse.}}
# An [[employee]] whose position in a [[corporate]] hierarchy is below that of a particular manager.
#: {{synonyms|en|subordinate}}

